      "message": "Looks like it works if you do the following:\n\n diff --git a/util/compare_build.sh b/util/compare_build.sh\nindex 56f7e0b0b..201d7c96d 100755\n--- a/util/compare_build.sh\n+++ b/util/compare_build.sh\n@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ DEFINE_string \u0027jobs\u0027 \"\" \u0027Number of jobs to pass to make\u0027 \u0027j\u0027\n # If you don\u0027t have more than 32GB, you probably don\u0027t want to run in parallel.\n DEFINE_string \u0027parallel\u0027 \"yes\" \\\n                 \u0027Make both refs at the same time (extreme mem usage)\u0027 \u0027p\u0027\n+DEFINE_boolean \u0027booltest\u0027 \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" \u0027testing bool\u0027\n \n # Process commandline flags.\n FLAGS \"${@}\" || exit 1\n@@ -53,6 +54,14 @@ parse_bool() {\n   esac\n }\n \n+if [[ \"${FLAGS_booltest}\" \u003d\u003d \"${FLAGS_TRUE}\" ]]; then\n+  echo \"booltest true\"\n+else\n+  echo \"booltest false\"\n+fi\n+\n+exit 0\n+\n KEEP_TEMP_DIR\u003d\"$(parse_bool \"${FLAGS_keep}\")\"\n PARALLEL\u003d\"$(parse_bool \"${FLAGS_parallel}\")\"\n\n\n\nThe output:\n\n  ./util/compare_build.sh --booltest\n  booltest true\n \n  ./util/compare_build.sh --nobooltest\n  booltest false",
